text I arrive fifteen minutes before the time we agreed to meet.
text Kotomi isn't here yet.
text I figured she'd either be early or right on time. Either way, I'm not worried about it.
text I lean against the wall and wait for her.
text @[Tomoya]
text ...
text It's so peaceful here.
text The sky is clear and I can hear birds singing.
text There are a few clouds floating high in the sky.
text I decide to look around to make sure Kyou isn't hiding anywhere.
text @[Tomoya]
text I let things slide yesterday, but I'll be sure to slap the crazy out of her today.
text @[Tomoya]
text ...
text @[Tomoya]
text And just where do you plan on slapping her, you perv?!
text @[Tomoya]
text ...
text I make a retort to my own stupid dirty joke, but there's no response.
text @[Tomoya]
text All right. Today's date will be fun. A true date with just the two of us.
text @[Tomoya]
text No comedic retorts today.
text @[Tomoya]
text Yeah, right!
text @[Tomoya]
text ...
text No response to the stupid remark.
text Now I feel a little sad.
text I get tired of the one man show and keep an eye on the street that Kotomi will be walking down.
text She should be here in the next five minutes or so.
text I stick my hands in my pockets and wait for her familiar footsteps.
text Something still feels off.
text Every time I try to wrap my head around it, I feel a pain in my chest. It feels like something is out of place.
text I look at my own shadow, cast by the bright sun.
text Something comes to mind for no reason.
text It's about the gentleman from the day before yesterday.
sound VYC.aac
text "If you see her, please convey a message for me."
sound VYD.aac
text "We still regret what we did that day."
text What did he mean?
text Should I tell Kotomi about it?
text I don't know the details, but I feel that nothing will change even if I bring it up.
text @[Tomoya]
text Phew...
text Realizing that my happy feelings are tainted, I sigh.
